<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ali Pasha of Yanina</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1740–<a href="/years/1822">1822</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Ali Pasha of Tepelena</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ali Pasha of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ioannina">Yanina</a> was an Albanian Ottoman governor who from 1788 ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/epirus">Epirus</a>, southern Albania and much of mainland <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a> from Ioannina. He built a near-independent state, dealt directly with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, and was visited by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lord-byron">Lord Byron</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahmud-ii">Mahmud II</a> moved against him in 1820, and his fall in 1822 helped make room for the Greek War of Independence.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ali-pasha-of-yanina.jpg" alt="Ali Pasha of Yanina" width="320" height="370" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Spyridon Ventouras · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ali_Pasha_Tepedelenli_by_Spyridon_Venturas_1818.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
